abstract: >-
  torch_vn_algebra is a Python library for batched computation with
  block-diagonal matrices in symmetry sectors, the finite-dimensional Type I
  von Neumann algebras (direct sums of matrix algebras), in PyTorch on CPU
  and GPU. It provides random operators with prescribed spectra and
  Haar-random unitaries, density matrices and entropies, quantum channels
  (Kraus, Choi, Stinespring) within and between sectors, tensor products with
  charge fusion and partial traces, Schrödinger and Lindblad dynamics, spin
  chains in U(1), momentum and SU(2) sectors with Lanczos and Krylov solvers,
  the numerical Wedderburn decomposition and commutant of the algebra
  generated by matrices or by a group representation, inclusions of algebras
  with conditional expectations and Jones indices, Jordan algebras, Petz and
  sandwiched Rényi divergences, and constrained batched optimisation, all
  differentiable with autograd. Self-contained lecture notes with complete
  proofs and a tested tutorial are included in seven languages.
